id: pm-jira-adf-block-evidence
title: Capture selected structured Jira description blocks as portable evidence
description: ""
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-29T03:46:37.895Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-29T04:15:12.222Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Table cell and code block round-trip with stable source coordinates; unsupported nodes are counted; changed source revision refuses approved capture.
comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T03:47:27.247Z",codex-agent,"Design: portable read-only capture packets preserve original RFC 6901 coordinates and ancestor scaffolding, never pull attachments or mutate native items. Approval compares both the caller-provided source revision and complete description digest, catching same-revision edits as well. Replay validates the exact producer schema and digest. No transaction isolation or remote freshness claim: callers supply a newly read source snapshot; this feature has no target writes, leases or frozen journal. Existing atomic replay work remains tracked separately by pm-jira-atomic-replay-revisions."
  "2026-10-29T03:53:18.949Z",codex-agent,"Implemented typed captureAdfEvidence/replayAdfEvidence plus jira capture-adf, with strict shared node schema, original JSON pointers, ancestor scaffolding, immutable copied attributes, digest/revision approval, complete exclusion counts and all-or-refuse output bounds. Added documented example and pm-evidence citation handoff. Seeded 500-sequence selection/approval property passed; native import/export/sync reference-model coverage now also asserts capture/replay against exact SDK readback. Targeted malformed-schema, sparse-array, CRLF, foreign packet and non-git CLI checks are in progress."
  "2026-10-29T03:58:20.664Z",codex-agent,"Real-data measurement used a read-only, non-git copy of public main at eaeaf48: 112 native items; exact SDK-read title/body-or-description projected into ADF table/code wrappers; 112 captures and round trips; 112 changed-revision refusals; 1680 source nodes, 560 retained nodes; 14825 native body bytes; 200704 emitted bytes, maximum packet 3996 bytes; zero budget refusals, zero Jira calls and unchanged SDK native state. This is real public tracker content in explicit ADF projections, not a live Jira validation."
  "2026-10-29T04:02:43.861Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: disposable non-git copies with only the source-revision guard disabled or original coordinates discarded both fail the table/code regression; the unchanged fixed implementation then passes. Pinned pm test --run --progress passed 9/9 focused tests with no skips. Typecheck, test compilation and docstrings pass. Full npm/Bun release checks remain assigned to CI at unchanged thresholds. Local health initially reports extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew in the preinstalled pm-github graph; refreshing the ignored project extension using the CI installation contract."
  "2026-10-29T04:03:51.238Z",codex-agent,"Focused coverage reports 100% lines, branches and functions in both new feature modules. All six real packed launch/install modes passed on host 2026.10.28 (24 mode assertions, one artifact): npm global, Bun global, npx, bunx, npm local and Bun local. Local strict tracker health now passes after refreshing pm-github exactly as CI does; only its ignored install graph changed and the managed registry timestamp was restored. Final packet-domain hardening narrows pointer indices and count bounds to producer domains; final exact-artifact acceptance will repeat after final generation."
  "2026-10-29T04:06:17.247Z",codex-agent,"Ready-for-review PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jira/pull/178 . Implementation commit d5fc6d8. Final source-domain hardening passes 7/7 core tests with 100% lines/branches/functions; installed no-git command previously passed 2/2, combined focused suite 9/9. Full unchanged-threshold npm/Bun release gates are running in the PR Node 22/26 CI matrix; exact-head evidence will be reported in the PR and handoff. Final generated-artifact acceptance is repeating all six installation modes. Existing atomic-import replay revision and interruption limitations remain out of this read-only feature scope and already have tracker items. No new SDK gap was encountered."
  "2026-10-29T04:12:11.795Z",codex-agent,"Exact-head CI at f0b2693 passed: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jira/actions/runs/40815913116 . Node 22 and 26 each passed npm run release:check and bun run release:check: 310/310 tests per gate, zero failures/skips, 100% lines/branches/functions across all 9 measured source files. Model diagnostics confirm 500 native sequences plus 2000 evidence operations and 40 safely refused older atomic replays. Final package SHA-256 9a37c667dda80f225b8761f7090cc6de183833780a2426ea0a9660a268bb5b45 passed all six install modes / 24 assertions. DeepScan identified one low-impact validation-script issue: an array used only as a counter. Replaced it with a numeric counter; production artifact bytes are unaffected. Final fresh CI will verify the follow-up head. Automated review availability: Sourcery/cubic quota-limited, Greptile trial ended, CodeRabbit skipped; these are not approvals."
  "2026-10-29T04:15:09.387Z",codex-agent,"Final official-ADF schema check identified a must-allow compatibility case: codeBlock may carry an empty marks array and block nodes may carry formatting marks. Widened only the new source boundary to accept bounded mark arrays on blocks; producers still discard block formatting and count omitted marks, and retained packets still disallow block marks. Added must-allow producer/replay regression including table-cell paragraph alignment and empty code-block marks. This preserves structure without exporting unwanted formatting data. Final artifact/CI acceptance will repeat for this source compatibility change."
